  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COD048N Goma Crisis DRA ACM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Subtitle" promeva:type="3" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goma Emergency Response</narrative>
  </description>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">six&#x2010;month emergency intervention in Sake, Kirotshe Health Zone, North Kivu, addressing the impact of the M23 insurgency that has displaced over 500,000 people since January 2025. The project, led by CARE and local partner KUA, targets 700 of the most food-insecure households (approximately 4,200 beneficiaries) by providing three rounds of emergency food assistance, while integrating protection activities to mitigate GBV risks.  Key Points:  Objectives: Stabilize food access through emergency distributions and improve protection by integrating GBV awareness and referral services.  Approach: A Rapid Gender Analysis (RGA) will inform beneficiary selection, prioritizing pregnant and lactating women, children under five, female-headed households, and persons with disabilities. Food distributions will be conducted at secure, community-designated sites with continuous monitoring.  Budget: With direct costs of &#x20ac;443,150 (totaling &#x20ac;481,685 with indirect costs), the project allocates 74% of funds to local partners.</narrative>
  </description>
