     <actual value="4858">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 10% overrun compared to the initial target is explained by a planning assumption based on an average household size of 6 persons. However, field observations, particularly in the Sake area, have revealed that many households have a higher than average number of children. This situation led to 115% of the forecasts being achieved, thus generating an estimated 7% deviation from the initial calculations.</narrative>
